    "overview": "Say и tell оба передают информацию, но tell обычно требует object — человека, которому что-то сообщают.",
    "main_rule": "Say focuses on words/message. Tell focuses on communicating to someone and usually takes an object in this reporting pattern.",
    "form": "say something / say that...\ntell someone something / tell someone to do something\ntell the truth / tell a story / tell a joke / tell the time",
    "when_why": "Сначала определи, назван ли receiver of message.",
    "examples": "She said that she was tired. → Она сказала, что устала.\nShe told me that she was tired. → Она сказала мне, что устала.\nHe told us the truth. → Он сказал нам правду.\nHe told a joke. → Он рассказал шутку.\nTell me the time, please. → Скажи мне, который час.",
    "special_cases": "После tell действительно часто называют получателя, но не всегда. Устойчивые сочетания tell the truth, tell a lie, tell a story, tell a joke, tell the time употребляются без него.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ He said me the truth. → ✅ He told me the truth.\n❌ He told me to the truth. → ✅ He told me the truth.\n❌ She told that she was tired. → ✅ She said that she was tired. / She told me that she was tired.\n❌ He said a joke. → ✅ He told a joke.",
    "dont_confuse": "say = words/message.\ntell = tell someone.",
    "quick_summary": "say something.\nsay that...\ntell someone something.\ntell someone to do."
